  "blueprint_md": "# Automation blueprint: Warranty claims from installers\n\n## Process summary\n\n- **Description:** A manufacturer of zoned HVAC controls sells through distributors and installers. Installers send warranty claims for faulty thermostats, dampers and control boards; aftersales checks eligibility, diagnoses the fault remotely and issues a return or a replacement.\n- **Owner:** Aftersales Service\n- **Executions per month:** 320\n- **Steps:** 7\n- **Analysis:** <timestamp>, process version 1, rules scoring-v1, LLM ok (fake/fake-deterministic-v1)\n\n## Current state\n\n- **Monthly hours:** 180.00\n- **Monthly cost:** 4,320.00\n\n## Automation opportunities\n\nOrdered by monthly time. Suitability measures whether a step can be automated, not how much it is worth.\n\n| # | Step | Method | Human control | Decided by | Hours/month | Suitability |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| 4 | Diagnose the fault remotely with the installer | HYBRID | REQUIRED | AI | 67.20 | 13 |\n| 2 | Check warranty eligibility | RULE_BASED | NONE | RULES | 26.67 | 95 |\n| 5 | Issue the RMA number and replacement order | RULE_BASED | NONE | RULES | 12.00 | 95 |\n| 3 | Ask the installer for missing documents | HYBRID | NONE | AI | 9.60 | 70 |\n| 7 | Approve the credit note or free replacement | RULE_BASED | REQUIRED | RULES | 7.20 | 65 |\n\n- **Diagnose the fault remotely with the installer:** Input is mixed and integration readiness is none.\n- **Check warranty eligibility:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n- **Issue the RMA number and replacement order:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n- **Ask the installer for missing documents:** Input is mixed and integration readiness is partial.\n- **Approve the credit note or free replacement:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n\n## Proposed architecture\n\n- Workflow engine that runs the steps in order, with retries and an audit log\n- Rules step in the workflow engine with explicit, versioned validation rules\n- Automated draft with a person confirming the result\n- Human review queue: flagged items wait for a decision, which is logged\n- Orchestrate the automated steps from a single workflow engine with retries\n- Route low-confidence and flagged items to a human review queue\n\n## Business impact\n\nEvery economic figure below depends on the assumptions listed after it.\n\n- **Hours freed per month:** 86.40\n- **Gross monthly savings:** 2,073.60\n- **Monthly tooling cost:** 50.00\n- **Net monthly savings:** 2,023.60\n- **Implementation cost:** 6,000.00\n- **Payback (months):** 2.97\n- **ROI at 12 months:** 305 %\n\n**Assumptions**\n\n- Implementation cost: 6,000.00\n- Monthly tooling cost: 50.00\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-1>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-2>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-3>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-4>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-5>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-6>: 50 %\n- 1 step(s) have no expected reduction and count as zero savings\n\n## Risks\n\n- [RULES / DATA] Register the claim from the installer handles sensitive data\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Diagnose the fault remotely with the installer depends on human judgement\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Inspect the returned unit in the lab depends on human judgement\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Approve the credit note or free replacement is business critical\n- [AI / OPERATIONAL] Exceptions need an owner once the happy path is automated\n\n## Human controls\n\n- **Register the claim from the installer:** REQUIRED. handles sensitive data; Reviewer decision: Reviewer keeps this step manual\n- **Diagnose the fault remotely with the installer:** REQUIRED. requires human judgement\n- **Inspect the returned unit in the lab:** REQUIRED. requires human judgement\n- **Approve the credit note or free replacement:** REQUIRED. requires human approval\n\n## Workflow specification\n\n1. Trigger: a new process execution starts\n2. Register the claim from the installer: MANUAL, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n3. Check warranty eligibility: RULE_BASED\n4. Ask the installer for missing documents: HYBRID\n5. Diagnose the fault remotely with the installer: HYBRID, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n6. Issue the RMA number and replacement order: RULE_BASED\n7. Inspect the returned unit in the lab: MANUAL, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n8. Approve the credit note or free replacement: RULE_BASED, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n9. End: record the outcome and the time spent for later comparison\n",
